.TH RUN 1 "2026" "Cyberus Linux Quest" "Mission 02 Manual"
.SH NAME
run \- Cyberus Mission 02 Home Sweet Home challenge binary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /challenge/run
.I /home/student/<output-file>
.br
.B /challenge/run
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B /challenge/run
verifies that you can pass an absolute file path inside your home directory
.RB ( /home/student )
and writes the Stage A verification record and your secret Stage B note phrase into that file.
.PP
Note: Bash builtin commands such as
.B cd
and
.B pwd
use
.B help cd
whereas external binaries like
.B run
use
.B man run
or
.BR "/challenge/run --help" .
.SH EXAMPLES
Since the shell expands
.B ~
to
.BR /home/student ,
you can run:
.PP
.nf
.RS
/challenge/run ~/stage_a.txt
cat ~/stage_a.txt
.RE
.fi
